# Project Structure Template

Purpose:
  This directory contains schemas, indexes, and routing tables for the
  project model. Concrete project data and templates are NOT stored here.

Contents:
  This directory is SCHEMA-ONLY. For reusable templates, see:
    @../../templates/INDEX.sdd

  Template sources:
    docs/
      00-about/project.template.md       — Project overview template
      20-architecture/overview.template.md — Architecture overview template
      INDEX.sdd                           — Docs routing
      mappings.sdd                        — Doc-to-sdd mappings
      ownership.sdd                       — Doc ownership rules

    decisions/
      INDEX.sdd                           — Decision index
      DEC-000.template.sdd                — Decision template

    tasks/
      INDEX.sdd                           — Task index
      TASK-000.template.sdd               — Task template

    stack/
      INDEX.sdd                           — Stack index
      LAYER.template.sdd                  — Stack layer template

    architecture/
      INDEX.sdd                           — Architecture index
      system.template.md                  — System architecture template

Usage:
  1. Templates are consumed from templates/_sdd/ by the project-structure skill
  2. When a new project is initiated, the skill generates project/ from templates
  3. Replace placeholders with actual project content
  4. Create concrete decisions (DEC-001, DEC-002, etc.)
  5. Create concrete tasks (TASK-001, TASK-002, etc.)
  6. Populate stack/ with actual technology choices

Note:
  This directory does NOT contain concrete project data.
  Concrete project data lives in:
    - prompt/ (human prompts)
    - .sdd/decisions/ (concrete decisions)
     - project/ (concrete code, generated from templates)

State: +
